<title>DENMARK: Denmark says market determines gold reserve value.</title>
<headline>Denmark says market determines gold reserve value.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's central bank said on Friday that the question of following Germany's plans to revalue gold reserves did not apply in its case as its reserves were valued annually according to prevailing market rates.</p>
<p>A bank official said reserves were valued at end-1996 at 3.7 billion crowns. --Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
